message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "vlm-cpu-benchmark: A Fair CPU-Only Efficiency and Quantization Benchmark for Small Vision-Language Models"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible, CPU-only benchmarking framework for small vision-language
  models. It measures per-inference latency, peak memory, and best-effort RAPL
  energy on fixed hardware, with each model run through its native preprocessing
  under identical greedy decoding, across fp32 and custom ONNX INT8 backends, on
  DocVQA, OCRBench, and a shared binary object-presence task that also compares
  the VLMs against CPU object detectors in closed- and open-vocabulary regimes.
type: software
